# Foliage is leaf cards, not a lobed solid (src/models/props/kit.gd `canopy`,
# src/render/foliage/leaf.gdshader). Played through the real game, seed 7 --
# the canon's -- so frames 01-03 stand beside canon 02, 04 and 08.
#
# The frames this tour exists for are 05 and 07: a machine among the leaves at
# play zoom, where it still reads. A canopy that hides a threat is a worse game
# however beautiful the frame, and no test can make that claim.
#   tools/tour.sh tours/foliage.tour --seed=7
#   tools/tour.sh tours/foliage.tour --seed=7 --quality=web   (the web tier's row;
#   the web RENDERER is only proved by tools/check.sh --web)
weather clear:0
place coast
wait 0.8
shot 01-coast-scrub with land:coast
place coast-pinewood
wait 0.8
shot 02-broadleaf-and-pine with border:coast-pinewood
# What the leaves cost, shown and hidden in turn inside this one run: fps taken
# across two runs of one command came back 83 and 63 on this machine.
perf foliage 3.0
place pinewood
wait 0.8
shot 03-pinewood-needles with land:pinewood
perf foliage 3.0
# Under a crown: it opens over the player, cut in stipple where the leaves are
# in the way, and nowhere else.
near broadleaf
wait 0.6
shot 04-under-a-crown with prop:broadleaf
# A machine walks in among the leaves. Its crown opens too.
spawn watcher
await mob:watcher 6
wait 0.6
shot 05-machine-among-the-leaves with mob:watcher,prop:broadleaf
# The pines: the wood the depth layer roofs with boughs, and the needles under it.
place pinewood
near pine
wait 0.4
spawn runner
await mob:runner 6
wait 0.6
shot 06-runner-under-the-needles with mob:runner,prop:pine
# Scrub is low and never opens, so a body behind a bush has to read over it.
place coast
near bush
wait 0.4
spawn harvester
await mob:harvester 6
wait 0.6
shot 07-harvester-past-the-scrub with mob:harvester,prop:bush
# The light through a canopy: a low sun behind the leaves.
place coast-pinewood
near broadleaf
hour 18.4
wait 1.0
shot 08-low-sun-through-a-crown with prop:broadleaf
# Snow is the leaves' own now (leaf.gdshader): lumps lying on the sprays that
# face the sky, and the needles cut through them, where a white tier laid over
# each bough was a sliver of paper. The snowfield at the hour the canon takes it,
# and then one laden pine close enough to see what holds the snow up.
hour 8
place snowfield
wait 1.0
shot 09-snowfield-under-snow with land:snowfield,prop:snow_pine
near snow_pine
zoom 6
wait 0.8
shot 10-a-laden-pine with prop:snow_pine
zoom 12
# The scrapwood: a sheet of the machine's plate caught in every crown, which is
# the whole of what says these trees grew through salvage. It faced the ground
# and was culled for the life of the model, so nothing was ever there to see.
hour 11
place scrapwood
wait 1.0
shot 11-scrapwood-plate-in-the-crowns with land:scrapwood,prop:scrap_tree
near scrap_tree
zoom 6
wait 0.8
shot 12-grown-through-salvage with prop:scrap_tree
zoom 12
weather rules
